Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an incorrect conditional check in the `marvell_suspend` and `marvell_resume` functions, where the code was checking if fiber mode was *not* supported instead of checking if it *was* supported. This led to situations where the PHY would attempt to suspend and resume fiber mode even when it was not supported, resulting in improper handling of the PHY modes.

